Kaomoji expression data is adapted from rimeinn/rime-kaomoji, revision
e66d8f26ee47b4a2a840983b7d71ed69b5ecf756, under LGPL-3.0.
The adaptation preserves expression spacing, adjusts categories and adds greeting
and sleep entries. Both original data and the adapted KaomojiCatalog.kt source
are distributed under assets/expressions/ in the APK. Its license texts are in
LICENSES/rime-kaomoji-LGPL-3.0.txt and LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt.

The experimental short-word scorer and separate developer benchmark use ONNX
Runtime 1.26.0 from Microsoft Corporation under MIT; see
LICENSES/onnxruntime-MIT.txt and LICENSES/onnxruntime-ThirdPartyNotices.txt.
The offline Chinese handwriting recognizer bundles PaddlePaddle's
PP-OCRv5_mobile_rec_onnx graph and derived character table, revision
ed152b8b495f84de93cda5709d768548a9127622. Its model card declares
Apache-2.0; see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt and THIRD_PARTY.md. It reuses the
already bundled ONNX Runtime without a runtime network download.
The bundled Mini INT8 graph is adapted from UER's
roberta-mini-wwm-chinese-cluecorpussmall, revision
5e567169018f5cf84cf1d85a2b391c8d51211eda. Conversion exports masked-position
log-probabilities and dynamically quantizes MatMul/Gather weights.
The project uses the UER Apache-2.0 licensing basis explicitly confirmed by the
maintainer; see https://github.com/dbiir/UER-py and LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
The independent model card has no weight-license metadata. This notice records
the project decision, not an additional upstream statement. Tiny/FP16 research
graphs and host tools (including ONNX under Apache-2.0) are not bundled.

English glide spellings are derived from Carnegie Mellon University's CMUdict,
revision 74790861f652b15e4ac49015a90074ad62a27690. Pronunciations and variant markers
are removed and spellings are filtered, deduplicated and sorted. The complete
BSD-style notice is preserved in LICENSES/cmudict-LICENSE.txt.

Unicode Emoji 18.0 sequences and CLDR 48 annotations are provided under Unicode
License V3. Bundled Noto Emoji artwork is adapted to lossless WebP from revision
e20cbc2bbec1926686be9f9bee7d1d2cfa1fea0e. Artwork attribution, flag terms and the
upstream OFL license text are preserved in LICENSES/ and assets/emoji/licenses/.
No Noto font binary is included. Sources and exact hashes are recorded in
tools/emoji/sources.lock.json and docs/rgi-emoji-validation.md.

The stroke recognizer adapts Zinnia's feature/scoring algorithm,
Copyright (c) 2005-2007, Taku Kudo, under BSD-3-Clause. It uses repacked Tegaki 0.3
simplified-light and traditional Chinese model data under LGPL-2.1. See
LICENSES/Zinnia-BSD-3-Clause.txt and LICENSES/Tegaki-LGPL-2.1.txt. The corresponding
source distribution contains the original training XML, model archives, build
files and the format-adaptation scripts. See SOURCES.md for replacement steps.
Wanxiang dictionaries and the RIME-LMDG simplified Chinese grammar model are
created by amzxyz and upstream contributors, distributed under CC BY 4.0.
